Here's an example of how you can use the getBoundingClientRect() method to get the bounding rectangle of an element:

```javascript
// Get the element
const element = document.getElementById('myElement');

// Get the bounding rectangle of the element
const rect = element.getBoundingClientRect();

// Access the properties of the rectangle
const x = rect.x; // Top-left x-coordinate of the rectangle
const y = rect.y; // Top-left y-coordinate of the rectangle
const width = rect.width; // Width of the rectangle
const height = rect.height; // Height of the rectangle
```

The bounding rectangle of the element is returned as an object with the properties x, y, width, and height, which can be used to determine the size and position of the element on the page.

